A shopping agent wants to end without buying because it thinks nothing fits. Check the listing records shown against the requirements, with these reading rules: the listing's attribute for a property decides when its key names that same property (any key spelling, one element of a list is enough, synonyms and unit conversions count, a value containing the required value's words counts, such as "deep teal" for teal, limits include the edge); a key for a different property, even a related one (a handle colour is not the body's colour), decides nothing; when no attribute names that property, the wanted value stated under another attribute or in the title or description counts (a bare figure that does not say what it measures counts for nothing); a requirement the category label itself states is met by that category; the category label must match the item; a rule of being unlike another listing's value counts as met unless the records show that same value; out-of-stock listings and listings that break the budget do not fit.
Records marked ROW were seen only as a search result row: their page (the attributes) has not been read, so they can be neither passed nor failed on a property the row does not show.
Return ONE JSON object and nothing else: {"fits": {"item number": [listing ids that appear to meet every requirement, cheapest first, at most 4]}, "open": [ids of ROW listings of a requested kind, inside the budget, whose page could show that they fit, most promising first, at most 6], "reason": "one sentence"}

REQUEST:
Gonna start with skirts, and the waist has to be an elasticated waist (I'll double-check that myself, don't you worry), since a skirt that fights me all day is a steep climb I don't need. I tried a skirt unseen once and it clashed with my whole closet (lesson learned). And it's got to be something y'all really have on hand right now, not just listed on some website way off yonder. Now I need one for class and will squint at every photo's look like a ridge line. Price-wise, nothing over 510 cts (yes, every penny counts for me), y'all (student loans ain't gonna pay themselves). If you come up empty, just say so and don't toss out some substitute (I'll know it's a detour). Total, you can send me 3 messages and no more than that. Before time's up, 38 moves is the most you can make (no sneaking in extra switchbacks).

REQUIREMENTS IN FORCE:
- item: skirt for class, quantity 1; requirements: waist: elasticated waist; pattern: matching stripe; shopper does not mind: look, colour
- budget: at most 510 cents in total
- pick: any listing that fits everything
- in stock only
- wish (tie-breaker only): Skirt should not clash with the rest of my closet.
- rule from the request: Only items really on hand now, not web-only listings.
- rule from the request: Do not suggest substitutes when nothing fits.
- rule from the request: Send at most 3 messages to the shopper.
- rule from the request: Use no more than 38 steps or moves.
- rule from the request: Stay within the price limit of 510 cents.
- if nothing fits: end without naming or suggesting any listing
- listing attributes come from datasheet_for_item; view_listing show none; a listing's page (what a chain of pages or a page check means) is shown by view_listing

